# Save tokens / money (LiveBid)

## Reply
- Few short sentences. No recap, no “what else”, no launch nag unless asked.
- One task per turn. Stop when done. Do not offer next ideas unless asked.

## Tools (biggest cost)
- Prefer Ask / cheaper model for questions; Agent only when code must change.
- Grep/read 1–3 files max. No repo scans, subagents, or parallel research by default.
- No verify / e2e / staging / prisma generate / full restart unless asked.
- Do not poll terminals or re-check health after a known-good start.
- Ignore stale shell “task finished” notices if the app was intentionally restarted.

## Chats
- New chat when the topic changes (fetch ≠ bug ≠ feature).
- Long Agent chats burn tokens — keep feature work in short focused chats.
